WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.165
This is a fix link.

2
00:00:01.215 --> 00:00:04.640
The customer follows it step by step, and
tells you it worked.

3
00:00:09.173 --> 00:00:09.859
Hi, I'm Von.

4
00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:10.778
Here's FixLink.

5
00:00:10.828 --> 00:00:15.927
I do the fix once in my own browser, and
the extension records each click as a
step.

6
00:00:19.816 --> 00:00:23.509
Private details are blurred before
anything leaves the browser.

7
00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:26.361
Emails, card numbers, keys, even inside
iframes.

8
00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:30.619
In the editor, I tidy the wording and
reorder steps.

9
00:00:30.669 --> 00:00:33.873
The guide already looks like the
customer's brand, not mine.

10
00:00:40.131 --> 00:00:41.433
One click publishes it.

11
00:00:41.483 --> 00:00:44.549
The share panel shows exactly what the
customer gets.

12
00:00:44.599 --> 00:00:46.077
I copy a ready-made reply.

13
00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:51.832
I paste it into the ticket.

14
00:00:51.882 --> 00:00:53.404
No more long text replies.

15
00:00:57.582 --> 00:01:01.382
The customer gets one step at a time, with
progress, on any screen.

16
00:01:01.432 --> 00:01:03.336
At the end, they say if it worked.

17
00:01:10.482 --> 00:01:14.772
Back in FixLink, I see which guides fix
things, and which ones need a rewrite.

18
00:01:18.082 --> 00:01:23.075
Every guide also works for AI assistants,
so a customer's own AI can follow the same

19
00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:23.435
steps.

20
00:01:25.732 --> 00:01:27.685
Try the live example at the link below.
